.TH INTEGRATION-SEED 1 "July 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
integration:seed \- Bulk seed local SPP users into a specific integration target.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php integration:seed
.IR <app_name>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B integration:seed
command automates the mass migration and synchronization of the historical SPP user base into a newly attached external application.
.PP
For example, if your SPP application has been running for 2 years with 5,000 users, and you decide to install Magento today, Magento will have 0 users. By running this command, SPP will query the local spp_users table, extract the identities, and iteratively use the MagentoDriver to bulk-inject all 5,000 users natively into Magento.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B app_name
The alias of the registered target driver (e.g., magento, discourse).
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.B Filesystem Writes:
None.
.br
.B DB Interactions:
Performs a mass SELECT query on the local spp_users table.
.br
.B Outbound HTTP Calls:
Will generate outbound HTTP calls if the selected driver (e.g., Discourse) communicates via REST API rather than Native Bootstrapping.
